     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for an inpatient adult, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the higher dose doesn't give more pain relief. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nThe order should also come from a licensed prescriber, or be confirmed by one. I can't verify that here.\n\nIf you pass along the intended dose, I can enter it once a prescriber confirms it. Typical options are:\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO, 3\u20134 times daily**, for mild to moderate pain.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO, 4 times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 4 times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum, and it's usually given with food and for the shortest time needed.\n\nIf 1600 mg was meant as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter that. If the prescriber really does want the higher dose, they should place the order themselves and document why."
      }
     ],
